# Copy this file to .env and adjust the values for your machine.
#
# Only EXPO_PUBLIC_* variables reach the app, and they are bundled into it:
# anyone with the app can read them. Never put a secret here. Secrets (AI keys,
# SMTP credentials) live only in Supabase.
#
# Every variable here is read and validated in src/lib/env.ts.

# Which build this is. Allowed: development | production. Default: development.
EXPO_PUBLIC_APP_ENV=development

# The Supabase backend. Both are public values (the app bundle contains them). Set both or
# neither: with neither, the app starts but cannot reach a backend.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY must be a *publishable* key (sb_publishable_...).
# A secret key (sb_secret_...) is refused on purpose: it must never be in the app.
#
# Local stack (npm run db:start prints the URL and the publishable key). Ports here are
# 544xx, set in supabase/config.toml:
#   from the computer or an iOS simulator:  http://127.0.0.1:54421
#   from an Android emulator:               http://10.0.2.2:54421   (10.0.2.2 is the computer)
# Cloud project (Project Settings > API Keys, in the Supabase dashboard). Production builds
# must use https:
#   https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=http://10.0.2.2:54421
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_...
